{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01007",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 5.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.04,
      "end_seconds": 10.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.2,
      "end_seconds": 17.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.48,
      "end_seconds": 23.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 24.11,
      "end_seconds": 30.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "It's bleeding, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.6,
      "end_seconds": 35.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.35,
      "end_seconds": 42.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Sertraline. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day for my mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 43.22,
      "end_seconds": 51.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.01,
      "end_seconds": 54.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.33,
      "end_seconds": 58.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Ever since... since last Tuesday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.82,
      "end_seconds": 64.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 64.48,
      "end_seconds": 71.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.55,
      "end_seconds": 79.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Have you had difficulty bending the finger?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.71,
      "end_seconds": 83.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.95,
      "end_seconds": 89.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "So, would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.37,
      "end_seconds": 95.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "It feels mild to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.86,
      "end_seconds": 100.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "What about a numb fingertip, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.65,
      "end_seconds": 104.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.76,
      "end_seconds": 110.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.91,
      "end_seconds": 122.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "I'd give it a four, out of ten. It's a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.83,
      "end_seconds": 126.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How about weakness of the hand?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.12,
      "end_seconds": 132.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any weakness of the hand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.52,
      "end_seconds": 137.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Ah. So, any bite, fever, dirt in the wound or redness spreading?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.68,
      "end_seconds": 154.48,
      "duration_seconds": 14.8,
      "text": "No, no bite, no fever, no dirt in the wound. I did have a cut on my finger at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.66,
      "end_seconds": 159.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.5,
      "end_seconds": 166.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.9,
      "end_seconds": 170.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.35,
      "end_seconds": 173.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.44,
      "end_seconds": 180.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.48,
      "end_seconds": 183.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 184.32,
      "end_seconds": 191.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with trimethoprim."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.81,
      "end_seconds": 193.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.73,
      "end_seconds": 203.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.49,
      "end_seconds": 222.47,
      "duration_seconds": 16.98,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.14,
      "end_seconds": 243.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.86,
      "end_seconds": 249.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.22,
      "end_seconds": 254.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.1,
      "end_seconds": 262.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "I have anxiety, for nearly five years. I've had depression, yes. Eczema, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.19,
      "end_seconds": 267.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Ah. Okay, I can see anxiety in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 269.58,
      "end_seconds": 282.88,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 18, pulse 71, BMI works out to 37.9, weight 97 kilos, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, height 160 centimetres, pressure 128 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.82,
      "end_seconds": 285.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.47,
      "end_seconds": 290.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.34,
      "end_seconds": 306.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.76,
      "end_seconds": 309.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.39,
      "end_seconds": 333.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.38,
      "end_seconds": 356.14,
      "duration_seconds": 17.76,
      "text": "You can relax now. So, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury at this stage. An infected wound is also on my list. Another possibility is a tendon injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.12,
      "end_seconds": 359.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.44,
      "end_seconds": 382.58,
      "duration_seconds": 22.14,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury, and we'll know more once the an X-ray of the finger is back. I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the finger for laceration. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.65,
      "end_seconds": 386.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.55,
      "end_seconds": 412.42,
      "duration_seconds": 24.87,
      "text": "I'll start you on tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day. That's for tetanus prevention. Keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that. Let's review you in five days. So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.61,
      "end_seconds": 416.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}